WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.839
-You know, Germany has

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:08.216
with it’s history, with it’s responsibility

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:09.300
toward these wars

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.720
has something to add to that conversation.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.305
We cannot tell a hero’s journey.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.307
We cannot have a mission

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:18.351
that you have to do

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.020
and then, in the end you’re successful.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.647
A German soldier cannot come

00:00:22.647 --> 00:00:24.107
successful out of the movie.

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.568
-I’m so sorry.

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:28.486
-That the balance

00:00:28.486 --> 00:00:29.946
especially when you’re writing

00:00:29.946 --> 00:00:31.614
of knowing or hoping 

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:33.199
that you’re going to get

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.368
incredible actors to be in each of these parts.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.746
There is a part of your brain that is thinking

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:40.206
I want to justify each one of these people.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.624
-Because tonight,

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:42.917
in this very room,

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:44.252
a murder

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:45.295
will be committed.

00:00:45.295 --> 00:00:46.254
My murder.

00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:50.008
-The important thing about this film

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:52.677
is although it is about somebody

00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:54.345
who gets a 

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:56.890
a very gloomy diagnosis

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.142
it’s actually a film about

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:00.518
not about dying

00:01:00.518 --> 00:01:01.394
it is about living. 

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:02.771
-The results have come back.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.148
I’m afraid this time

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:06.357
they’re pretty conclusive.

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:09.319
It’s never easy, this.

00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:10.528
-Quite. 

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:13.406
-During the writing of the film

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.576
also during the shooting and in the editing of the film

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.536
we were, we found ourselves,

00:01:18.536 --> 00:01:21.414
time and again, leaning towards recreating

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.167
moments of the film and we found, time and again, that

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.753
the more we let go of the original movie

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:30.131
and went in our own direction the film became

00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:31.216
much more true.

00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:34.511
-The end is inevitable, Maverick.

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:36.262
Your kind is headed for extinction.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.139
-Maybe so, sir.

00:01:39.557 --> 00:01:41.017
But not today. 

00:01:43.311 --> 00:01:45.021
-When I see the film

00:01:45.021 --> 00:01:47.232
I’m able to kind of see all of our

00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:49.776
all of these little tendrils of different people’s

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.694
thoughts and dreams in the film

00:01:51.694 --> 00:01:53.279
and so, your sort of able to be proud of it

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.782
in a different way than if it was just your voice

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:56.866
and that’s been thrilling.

00:01:57.158 --> 00:01:58.660
-We know that we are bruised

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.161
and infected

00:02:00.411 --> 00:02:01.412
and pregnant

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:02.622
and terrified

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:03.289
and insane

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:03.789
and

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.375
some of us are dead!

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:06.918
-More than anything

00:02:06.918 --> 00:02:08.461
I just wanted to

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.796
be part of

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.422
 a really good story.

